ana-pilgrimage-circuit","n":"12.10.1","t":"Rāmāyaṇa Pilgrimage Circuit","l":3},{"id":"12102-mahabharata-pilgrimage-circuit","n":"12.10.2","t":"Mahābhārata Pilgrimage Circuit","l":3},{"id":"sec-archaeological_evidence","n":"12.11","t":"Archaeology, Astronomy and the Historicity of the Epics","l":2},{"id":"12111-sites-associated-with-the-ramayana","n":"12.11.1","t":"Sites Associated with the Rāmāyaṇa","l":3},{"id":"12112-sites-associated-with-the-mahabharata","n":"12.11.2","t":"Sites Associated with the Mahābhārata","l":3},{"id":"12113-astronomical-dating-of-the-war","n":"12.11.3","t":"Astronomical Dating of the War","l":3},{"id":"12114-medicine-and-material-culture","n":"12.11.4","t":"Medicine and Material Culture","l":3},{"id":"sec-global_influence","n":"12.12","t":"Global Influence and International Reception","l":2},{"id":"12121-the-bhagavad-gita-in-world-literature","n":"12.12.1","t":"The Bhagavad Gītā in World Literature","l":3},{"id":"12122-peter-brook-and-the-global-mahabharata","n":"12.12.2","t":"Peter Brook and the Global Mahābhārata","l":3},{"id":"12123-the-ramayana-in-world-literature","n":"12.12.3","t":"The Rāmāyaṇa in World Literature","l":3},{"id":"sec-contemporary_relevance","n":"12.13","t":"Contemporary Relevance and Living Tradition","l":2},{"id":"12131-the-nationalist-reception","n":"12.13.1","t":"The Nationalist Reception","l":3},{"id":"12132-academic-and-scholarly-engagement","n":"12.13.2","t":"Academic and Scholarly Engagement","l":3},{"id":"12133-postcolonial-and-feminist-re-readings","n":"12.13.3","t":"Postcolonial and Feminist Re-readings","l":3},{"id":"12134-the-epics-in-indian-classical-music","n":"12.13.4","t":"The Epics in Indian Classical Music","l":3},{"id":"sec-conclusion","n":"12.14","t":"Conclusion: The Epics as Living Tradition","l":2}]}]},{"name":"Back matter","items":[{"f":"bibliography.html","t":"Select Bibliography","w":724,"s":[]},{"f":"glossary-of-key-terms.html","t":"Glossary of Key Terms","w":315,"s":[]},{"f":"imagecredits.ht